{{$trigger := print `\A(?i)(?:\` .ServerPrefix `|<@!?` .BotUser.ID `>\*)(` .CCTrigger `)`}}
{{if not (reFind $trigger .Message.Content)}}
	{{return}}
{{end}}

{{/*
This is used to set ALL the data used within the system dynamically.
This includes but is not limited to morph data, discord ranks, roblox ranks

Changes here will not take affect until the command is re-run.
*/}}

{{/* Main subfaction data */}}
{{$baseData := sdict
	"EmbedColor" 4003205
	"RobloxGroupID" 36098297
	"NicknameRegex" "\\s\\|.*"
}}

{{/* Echelon, subdivision & rank role data */}}

{{/* Base morph data */}}
{{$baseMorphData := sdict
	"Shirt" 9326560199
	"Pants" 4607034531
	"RTagColour" "61 21 133"
	"StarterGear"  "bp-77,pistol"
}}

{{/*
Division / Echelon / Rank Data Structure

$data contains the complete organisational structure for
the faction system.

The hierarchy is stored directly instead of using separate
division, echelon, and rank lists.

Structure:

$data (cslice)
	|
	+-- Division (sdict)
		|
		+-- Echelons (cslice)
			|
			+-- Echelon (sdict)
				|
				+-- Ranks (cslice)
					|
					+-- Rank (sdict)
*/}}


{{/*
Division Definition

Each division is represented as an sdict with:

- "Name" (string)
	Full name of the division.
	Example: "Internal Cult Analysis Division"

- "ShortName" (string)
	Short identifier used internally.
	Example: "ICAD"

- "RoleID" (int)
	Discord role ID assigned to the division.

- "MorphData" (sdict, optional)
	Default morph configuration inherited by all
	child echelons and ranks.

- "Echelons" (cslice)
	Ordered list of echelon definitions belonging to
	this division.
*/}}

{{/* 
Echelon Definition

Each echelon is represented as an sdict with:
- "Name" (string)
	Full name of the echelon.
	Example: "Veil Command"

- "ShortName" (string)
	Internal identifier used by ranks and commands.
	Example: "VC"

- "RoleID" (int)
	Discord role ID assigned to the echelon.

- "MorphData" (sdict, optional)
	Additional morph configuration.

	Values override division-level MorphData.

- "Ranks" (cslice)
	Ordered list of rank definitions belonging to
	this echelon.
*/}}

{{/*
Rank Definition

Each rank is represented as an sdict with:

- "Name" (string)
	Full name of the rank.
	Example: "Warden Of The Veil"

- "ShortName" (string)
	Internal identifier used for rank commands
	and tags.
	Example: "Warden"

- "RoleID" (int)
	Discord role ID assigned to the rank.

- "MorphData" (sdict, optional)
	Additional morph configuration.

	Values override both division and echelon
	MorphData.

- "PromotionData" (sdict, optional)
	Defines automatic progression.

	Contains:

	- "DeploymentsRequired" (int)
		Number of deployments/trainings required.

	- "NextRankShortName" (string)
		ShortName of the rank to promote to.
*/}}

{{/*
Morph Inheritance

MorphData is inherited down the hierarchy:

Division MorphData
		|
		v
Echelon MorphData
		|
		v
Rank MorphData


Lower levels override higher levels.

Example:

Division:
	Shirt = A

Echelon:
	Hats = B

Rank:
	Health = 150

Final result:
	Shirt = A
	Hats = B
	Health = 150


---------------------------------------------------------
Ordering

Because cslices preserve order:

- Divisions should be listed in organisational order.
- Echelons should be listed from highest to lowest.
- Ranks should be listed according to progression order.

This ordering is used when generating database data.
*/}}

